"""How each score's definition was checked, kept beside the scores and shown by `describe`.

Each entry is (what the definition was read from, what the worked-example tests rest on). Wording is plain on purpose: a
definition read from a primary paper says so, one read only from a guideline, a textbook table or a calculator page says that,
and a part nobody could read is named. A score is not added to the registry without a line here
(test_clinical_scores.py holds the two together).

Worked-example kinds: SRC is an output printed in the source, REF an independent script's output computed while the
definition was being verified, HAND arithmetic done by hand from the definition.
"""

